{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Article I applies the agreement only to excess policies written \"excess of underlying insurance which afford limits not less than\" the Schedule of Underlying Limits, yet Article III (Retention and Reinsurance) expressly contemplates that the underlying Hospital Professional Liability limit may be \"self-insured\" rather than insured. Whether a self-insured retention or a state compensation fund satisfies Article I's underlying-insurance requirement cannot be answered from Article I alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.34},
   {"issue": "The enumerated coverage list (Commercial General Liability, Hospital Professional Liability, Automobile Liability, Non-Owned Aircraft and Heliport Liability) has no catch-all, so an excess policy insuring some other hospital-related exposure falls outside the cession. The scope of \"the REINSURED'S excess liability policies\" is defined only by that closed list.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Schedule requires $5,000,000 underlying Heliport Liability, while Article II(c) excludes loss arising out of the ownership, operation or use of helicopters owned or leased by the insured hospital. The two cannot easily both be given effect for a hospital with its own helicopter service.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause deems a discovery period or extended reporting endorsement part of the original policy period \"subject to the provision that a separete Limit of liability may apply in respect thereof,\" without saying who decides or when a separate limit applies. The permissive \"may apply\" leaves the reinsurer's exposure for a tail period indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause incorporates \"The Nuciear Incident Exclusion Clauses and the Insolvency Clause\" as attached, but the attached Nuclear Incident Exclusion Clause No. 2 refers to a \"Broad Exclusion Provision\" whose text does not appear anywhere in the instrument. What is incorporated is therefore incomplete on the face of the agreement.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Exclusion (a) turns on whether the insured operates a \"teaching hospital, childrenst hospital or psychiatric hospital,\" none of which is defined; a general hospital with residency programs or a pediatric unit may or may not qualify. The exclusion gives no test for how much teaching or pediatric activity makes a hospital one of the named kinds.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.46},
   {"issue": "Exclusions (a), (b) and (d) of this Article were deleted and replaced by Amendment No. 1 for policies becoming effective on or after July 1, 1995, so which version of the exclusion governs a given ceded policy depends on reading the two together. The original 250-bed and children's/psychiatric hospital exclusions cannot stand with the substituted 350-bed, teaching-hospital-only text.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The article's 90%/10% split applies only where \"the underlying Hospital Professional Liability limit of $1,000,000/$3,000,000 is self-insured,\" a term the agreement nowhere defines. Whether coverage through a captive, a state patients' compensation fund, or a retention endorsement counts as self-insured decides who bears the first $1,000,000.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Loss\" is confined to amounts \"within applicable policy limits as are actually paid by the REINSURED in settlement of claims or in Satisfaction of awards or judgments,\" which does not say whether sums paid in compromise of disputed or arguably uncovered claims qualify. The 90% sublimits in (b) and (c) further leave unclear how a single settlement is allocated between ordinary loss and extra-contractual loss.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Net salvage, subrogation or any other recovery (after expenses)\" does not identify which expenses are deducted or how recoveries are shared where loss straddles the retention. The catch-all \"any other recovery\" has no stated boundary.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
